--TEST--
`Core\Path::$m()` names a static property of a `Core` class, which no `Core` class declares, so it is `E0309` and not a method called by a name held in a variable
--FILE--
<?nvs
// PHP calls the method named by `$m`. Here `Core\Path::$m` is a static
// property, and a `Core` class has none.
string $m = 'basename';
echo Core\Path::$m('a/b'), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0309]: `Core\Path` has no static property named `m`
  --> case.nvs:5:6
